            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Before the new one: say the Persian for to be well cooked, then the Persian for a slotted spoon."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: زعفران",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "زعفران (za'farân) — \"saffron\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "زعفران (za'farân) به برنج رنگ زرد میدهد. Za'farân be berenj rang-e zard midahad. Saffron gives rice a yellow colour."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "It is brewed first in a little hot water, then poured over the rice."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "za'farân is borrowed from Arabic za'farān, \"saffron\" (EtymDB), and EtymDB links the Arabic word in turn with a Persian zarparān, \"with golden leaves\"."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "One more word for telling, explaining and describing at B1."
