          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "اضافه کردن (ezâfe kardan) — \"to add\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "در آخر کمی نمک اضافه کرد. Dar âkhar kami namak ezâfe kard. At the end she added a little salt."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "With be: be khoresh ezâfe kard. Ezâfe is also the name of the Persian linking -e."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ezâfe is borrowed from Arabic iḍāfa, \"an adding, an adjunct\" (EtymDB). kardan \"to do\" is inherited Persian."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
